[align=center]
[size=200][b]Advanced — Custom Lovelace & YAML Dashboard[/b][/size]
[color=#5B8DEF][i]For custom layouts, development and users who deliberately want manual dashboard control[/i][/color]
[/align]
[hr]
[notice]The automatic Native Switch Vision sidebar dashboard is the recommended workflow. Manual Lovelace/YAML remains supported as an advanced fallback.[/notice]

Discovery writes generated card configuration to:
[code]/share/switch_vision/generated-dashboard-card.yaml[/code]

A manual dashboard must register:
[code]/local/switch-vision/js/switch-vision.js?v=<current-core-version>[/code]
Generated manual layouts using Layout Card also require:
[code]/hacsfiles/lovelace-layout-card/layout-card.js[/code]
The Native panel does not require either manual resource entry.

[size=150][b]Typical card type[/b][/size]
[code]type: custom:switch-vision-3650[/code]
Despite the historical card-type name, model-aware registry information determines the actual supported switch presentation.

[size=150][b]Do not hand-maintain generated identity[/b][/size]
Discovery owns generated entity prefixes, model information and generated card bindings. Keep manual custom copies separate from Discovery's generated file.
